Supreme People's Court

Notice on the Trial of Cases Involving Layout Designs of Integrated Circuits

(Adopted at the 1197th Meeting of the Adjudication Committee of the Supreme People's Court on October 30, 2001)

Fa Fa [2001] No. 24

To: the High People's Courts of all provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities directly under the Central Government; the Military Court of the People's Liberation Army; and the Production and Construction Corps Branch of the High People's Court of Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region

The Regulations on the Protection of Layout Designs of Integrated Circuits of the State Council came into effect as of October 1, 2001. Providing judicial protection for the exclusive rights in layout designs of integrated circuits is a new trial task for the people's courts. Performing this trial work well will be of great significance for protecting the legitimate rights and interests of holders of layout design rights, encouraging innovation in integrated circuit technology, and promoting the development of science and technology.

To ensure that the people's courts lawfully accept and fairly adjudicate cases involving layout designs of integrated circuits (hereinafter referred to as layout designs), in accordance with the relevant provisions of the Civil Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China, the Administrative Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China, and the Regulations on the Protection of Layout Designs of Integrated Circuits, notice on relevant issues concerning the trial of layout design cases is hereby given as follows:

I. Scope of Accepted Cases

The people's courts shall accept the following cases involving layout designs that meet the conditions for filing a lawsuit as stipulated in Article 108 of the Civil Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China and Article 41 of the Administrative Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China:

(1) Disputes over the ownership of exclusive rights in a layout design;
(2) Disputes over contracts for the transfer of exclusive rights in a layout design;
(3) Disputes over infringement of exclusive rights in a layout design;
(4) Cases concerning applications for pre-litigation orders to cease infringement and for property preservation;
(5) Cases against the reconsideration decision of the intellectual property administrative department of the State Council rejecting an application for registration of a layout design;
(6) Cases against the decision of the intellectual property administrative department of the State Council revoking the registration of a layout design;
(7) Cases against the decision of the intellectual property administrative department of the State Council regarding a non-voluntary license to use a layout design;
(8) Cases against the ruling of the intellectual property administrative department of the State Council concerning the remuneration for a non-voluntary license to use a layout design;
(9) Cases against the decision of the intellectual property administrative department of the State Council on handling infringement of exclusive rights in a layout design;
(10) Cases against the administrative reconsideration decision of the intellectual property administrative department of the State Council;
(11) Other cases involving layout designs.

II. Jurisdiction over Cases

The categories of cases listed in items (5) through (10) of Article I of this Notice shall be tried by the Beijing No. 1 Intermediate People's Court as the court of first instance. The remaining categories of cases shall be tried by the intermediate people's courts in the localities where the people's governments of provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities directly under the Central Government are situated, in the localities of special economic zones, and in the cities of Dalian, Qingdao, Wenzhou, Foshan, and Yantai as the courts of first instance.

III. Application of Pre-litigation Measures for Ordering Cessation of Relevant Acts

Where an application is made to the people's court for a pre-litigation order to cease infringement of exclusive rights in a layout design, the provisions of the Several Provisions of the Supreme People's Court on Issues Concerning the Application of Laws to Pre-litigation Cessation of Patent Infringement shall be applied by reference.

IV. Suspension of Proceedings

Where, in a dispute over infringement of exclusive rights in a layout design accepted by a people's court, the defendant requests suspension of the proceedings on the ground that the plaintiff's exclusive right in the layout design lacks sufficient stability, the people's court generally shall not suspend the proceedings.

All high and intermediate people's courts shall organize relevant trial personnel to earnestly study and research the Regulations on the Protection of Layout Designs of Integrated Circuits, to become familiar with and master the relevant legal theories and professional knowledge, and to diligently improve the professional competence and judicial level of trial personnel. They shall actively carry out investigation and research on cases involving layout designs and promptly summarize trial experience. Legal documents issued in final adjudications of cases involving layout designs shall be promptly submitted to the Supreme People's Court.

November 16, 2001
